       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. The dose needs checking first.\n\n**The problem:** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily adds up to **5100 mg/day**. The maximum is **2550 mg/day** for immediate-release and 2000 mg/day for extended-release. This order is about twice the maximum, which raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI side effects even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**Common regimens this might have been meant to be:**\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2550 mg/day, the maximum for IR)\n- **850 mg PO twice daily** (1700 mg/day total)\n- **1700 mg/day total**, split into doses\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, including whether it's immediate- or extended-release, and I'll enter it. If you really do mean 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and give a reason, and I'll put it in the order note."
